 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "부가의문문 (question tags)",
   "en": "question tags: isn't it?, don't you?, can't she?"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "부가의문문은 문장 끝에 붙여 확인하거나 동의를 구하는 짧은 의문문입니다. 긍정문에는 부정 꼬리(isn't it?), 부정문에는 긍정 꼬리(is he?)를 붙입니다. 조동사나 be동사는 그대로, 일반동사는 do / does / did를 씁니다. 대답은 사실이 맞으면 Yes, 아니면 No로 합니다.",
   "en": "A question tag is a short question added to a sentence to check or ask for agreement. Use a negative tag after a positive sentence (isn't it?) and a positive tag after a negative sentence (is he?). Use the same auxiliary or be; with other verbs use do / does / did."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "긍정 → 부정",
     "It's a nice day, isn't it?"
    ],
    [
     "부정 → 긍정",
     "He isn't a student, is he?"
    ],
    [
     "일반동사 / do",
     "You like coffee, don't you?"
    ],
    [
     "조동사 / modal",
     "You can swim, can't you?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "긍정문 + 부정 꼬리 / 부정문 + 긍정 꼬리.",
    "en": "Positive sentence + negative tag; negative sentence + positive tag."
   },
   {
    "ko": "일반동사 현재 → don't / doesn't, 과거 → didn't.",
    "en": "Present → don't / doesn't; past → didn't."
   },
   {
    "ko": "꼬리의 주어는 대명사: it, he, she, you.",
    "en": "The tag subject is a pronoun: it, he, she, you."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "It's a nice day, isn't it?",
    "ko": "오늘 날씨가 좋네요, 그렇죠?"
   },
